//
// A SET MISSING A VARIANT, WITHOUT AN ENUM-LEVEL MEMBER, IS REFUSED AT THE CALL
// (`@FR-Disp-Dynamic`'s last sentence, in `M-Exhaust`'s shape; `@FR-Disp-Exhaustive` says no
// "no applicable method" path exists at run time).  `dm(DFire)` and `dm(DIce)` cover two of
// three variants and no member is declared at `DEnt`, so a call with a `DEnt`-held argument
// would have no leaf for `DRock`: refused naming the missing tuple and the members declared.
// One refusal per file.
//
// @falsified-at: none — a conformance guard; the refusal fired as expected on 18594597b,
//   interpret and native.
// CHANNEL: the compile (the expected diagnostic).
// ARMED: no instrument.
// WITNESS: the diagnostic names the uncovered variant and the declared members.
// HOLDS: a static call at `DFire` is not refused — the refusal is the enum-held call's.
// @EXPECT_ERROR: `dm(DEnt)` has no definition for the pair (DRock) — declared: dm(DFire), dm(DIce)

enum DEnt { DFire { n: integer }, DIce { n: integer }, DRock { n: integer } }

fn dm(a: DFire) -> text { "fire {a.n}" }
fn dm(a: DIce) -> text { "ice {a.n}" }

fn main() {
  println(dm(DFire { n: 0 }));
  x: DEnt = DFire { n: 1 };
  println(dm(x));
}
